==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|That was on location, and I always enjoy it when Star Wars goes on location. It sort of adds a different sort of slant to the whole thing.|Hayden Christensen discussing filming a scene as Anakin Skywalker in a vision|<ref name="Sweet gesture">{{WebCite|url=https://www.cinemablend.com/interviews/obi-wan-kenobis-hayden-christensen-talks-wearing-the-anakin-costume-again-and-ewan-mcgregors-sweet-gesture|text=Obi-Wan Kenobi's Hayden Christensen Talks Wearing The Anakin Costume Again And Ewan McGregor's 'Sweet' Gesture|author=Hurley, Laura|date=2022-06-15|work=[https://www.cinemablend.com CinemaBlend]|archivedate=20220615135029}}</ref>}}
Mapuzo was first pictured in the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the teaser trailer for ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'', a [[2022]] [[Disney+]] television series. It was first mentioned in "[[Part II]]" of the series,<ref name="Kenobi II" /> which aired on [[May 26]], 2022.<ref name="Episode 2 Premiere">{{Twitter|obiwankenobi|status/1530019678562549760|''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]''|quote=The time for #ObiWanKenobi has arrived&hellip;early. Start streaming the first two episodes on @DisneyPlus TONIGHT at 9PM PT.|archivedate=20220527053945}}</ref> It first appeared in the [[Part III|third episode]] of the series, which was released on [[June 1]], 2022.<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-june-2022|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in June 2022}}</ref> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, Mapuzo was briefly mentioned in the context of a [[Mapuzo break-in|break-in]] that occurred there in ''[[Alliance Intelligence Reports]]'', a [[1995]] [[West End Games]] supplement<ref name="Part III guide">{{SW|url=series/obi-wan-kenobi/part-iii-guide|text=Part III Episode Guide &#124; Obi-Wan Kenobi}}</ref> to ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]'', although the sourcebook did not specify what Mapuzo was.<ref name="Alliance Intelligence Reports">''[[Alliance Intelligence Reports]]''</ref> The [[Mapuzo system/Legends|Mapuzo system]] was then mentioned in the [[2009]] reference book ''[[The Essential Atlas]]'', authored by [[Daniel Wallace]] and [[Jason Fry]].<ref name="TEA">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

The first scene shot with [[Hayden Christensen]] was when he played Anakin Skywalker in a vision seen by Kenobi<ref name="Sweet gesture" /> on Mapuzo.<ref name="Kenobi III" /> The scene was shot on location, and [[Ewan McGregor]],<ref name="Sweet gesture" /> the actor who played Kenobi,<ref name="Kenobi III" /> insisted on staying on the set to be part of Christensen's first shot back.<ref name="Sweet gesture" />

